The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 10 KB) but isn't committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit step's git add refused it and || true let it through. I briefly staged it with -f, then unstaged it, so the file is only on disk. That's probably what the harness expects.

State: the harness ran the build and tests at session start and they passed. I didn't re-run the suite. The binary round-trip works: yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: ok" returned ok with exit 0. The last 4 finished evolve runs succeeded, the trajectory shows 0 reverts in 14 days, and yoagent 0.27.2 is still the newest release.

For the planner:
1. Two files are close to the size limit, past which `cargo test` fails and the whole task reverts.
   • src/help.rs is 2946 lines against its recorded 2856. Ten more lines makes it fatal, and almost every user-facing task touches this file.
   • src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 2036 lines with no recorded entry. Fourteen more lines makes it fatal.

   The fix is cheap and protects every later task: split the files, or update their entries in tests/module_size.rs.
2. Non-interactive mode approves every tool call, and the docs don't say so. yoyo -p and piped stdin approve everything (src/main.rs:1395-1396, and src/cli.rs:1375, where --print implies --yes). Only the built-in hard-deny list and the user's own deny list stop anything.
   • Claude Code asks or refuses in the same situation, and its 2.1.319 release added a setting that refuses and carries on instead of waiting at a prompt.
   • Our docs never mention this behaviour, and docs/src/configuration/permissions.md shows yoyo -y -p as if -y were needed.
   • The evolve loop depends on this behaviour, and the script that sets it up is protected. So the safe step now is to state it in the docs. Whether to change the default is a question for @yuanhao.
3. #1114: yoyo -p --print-system-prompt prints the prompt instead of sending it. It's a real argument-parsing bug and has been open 5 days.
4. #1127 remainder: a bare yoyo docs still prints usage: /docs <crate>, which a shell can't run.
5. #1147: about 24 model ids we offer still have no outside source behind them. grok-3, which xAI retired in May, is a concrete next one.

The last 11 commits all sat in providers, presets and cost code. Items 1–4 are outside that area.

Research: I checked the vault first, then compared Claude Code 2.1.318 and 2.1.319 against the built binary. yoyo already handles three of the five items I checked:
• yoyo setup </dev/null exits 2 with "Nothing was written".
• Deny rules are checked before allow rules.
• Refusals already give non-zero exits.

